  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 1067769,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 0 - Gravity: A Commodore 64 Masterpiece\n\nPrepare for a mind-bending journey into the heart of a black hole in *0 - Gravity*, a revolutionary puzzle-action game for the Commodore 64.  Developed by Randy Wilson (of Macintosh *Continuum* fame), this unique title challenges players to manipulate gravity itself to navigate treacherous, abstract environments.\n\nYou control a lone astronaut trapped within a collapsing star system, tasked with collecting scattered energy orbs to power an escape vessel. The core mechanic involves rotating gravitational fields, altering the direction of your astronaut's movement and the trajectory of the orbs.  Mastering this mechanic is crucial, as you’ll need to strategically bend gravity to overcome obstacles, avoid deadly cosmic debris, and reach the exit portals.\n\n*0 - Gravity* boasts stunning, minimalist graphics and a haunting, atmospheric soundtrack that perfectly complements the game's unsettling premise.  Its innovative gameplay and challenging puzzles offer a truly unique and rewarding experience, pushing the boundaries of what’s possible on the Commodore 64.  Can you escape the pull of the black hole?"
    },
